> turbostat 3.0

Added RAPL support to turbostat, named it version 3,
and queued it for Linux 3.8 merge window.

"RAPL support" to most people means that "turbostat now prints Watts".
It actually knows about the full RAPL register set, which is useful
for people (like me) who are investigating RAPL's effectiveness
for power capping.

